====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}
{{tlb|en|computing}}

# {{sid|en|message system or service}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} A [[system]] for [[transmit]]ing and [[receive|receiving]] [[message#Noun|messages]] and [[data]] by means of a [[computer network]], primarily the [[Internet]], using the {{w|Simple Mail Transfer Protocol}} and the {{w|Internet Message Format}}.
#: {{syn|en|mail<id:email service>}}
#: {{ant|en|mail<id:postal service or system>|post#Noun|snail mail<id:postal service or system>}}
#: {{ux|en|He sent me his details via '''email'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The advent of '''email''' has simultaneously brought our society closer together and farther apart.}}
# {{sid|en|quantity of messages, mass sense}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[quantity]] of messages sent through an email system.
#: {{syn|en|mail<id:email messages, mass sense>}}
#: {{ant|en|mail<id:physical material conveyed by the postal service>|post#Noun|snail mail<id:physical material conveyed by the postal service>}}
#: {{ux|en|I am searching through my old '''email'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|My inbox used to allow only 50 MB of '''email''' at a time until last year, when they upgraded it to 2 GBs!}}
# {{sid|en|one message, count sense}} {{lb|en|countable}} A [[message]] being sent through email.
#: {{syn|en|mail<id:one email message>}}
#: {{ant|en|mailpiece#Noun}}
#: {{ux|en|He sent me an '''email''' last week to remind me about the meeting.}}
#: {{ux|en|I archive my old '''emails''' using a cloud-based service.}}
# {{sid|en|email address, informally}} {{lb|en|countable|informal}} {{clip of|en|email address}}.
#: {{ux|en|What’s your '''email'''?}}
#: {{ux|en|In this system, your username is your '''email'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Don’t send personal messages to my work '''email'''.}}

